  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SCC People to People Peace Forums</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 2-year project that Sudan Council Of Churches will embark on to promote conflict transformation and reconciliation in Southern Sudan and in the transitional regions of Southern Kodofan (Abyei &amp; Nuba mountains), and southern Blue Nile as well as in Nothern Sudan by engaging the conflict-affected regions and communities in dialogue.  The council through the proposed peace project will convene peace-building and reconciliation forum initiatives at the state, political leadership, church leadership and grassroots levels to engage different parties in the process of dialogue aimed at reconciling the different groups to forge necessary peace and co-existence during and in the post referendum era. This process has already been kick started by convening of Kajiko II forum that comprised of senior church leadership &amp; represnetatives and senior GoSS and State leadership as well as officials across the region. This is set to be followed by 12 regional conferences of which 20 Community Peace Committees are expected to be formed to promote and sustain peaceful relationships within and between the ethnic groups and provide them with an opportunity to reconcile and to develop agreements that will empower them to live together in peace. Inter faith forums will constitute part of these forums. CAFOD is committed to supporting the process by contributing towards these initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
